A||N||2||BlackDragon||aero front, how hard is it to instal on a non aero?||||1||
Z||000000||BlackDragon||11-08-2001||01:46 AM||||i said it all in the topic, but i will say again. how hard is it to put an aero front bumper on a non aero car? do they both have the same mounts? do you have to change the energy absorber? any other info i should have before i consider this? any help would be appreciated<P>------------------<BR>riced civics suck||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroBUZZ||11-08-2001||06:35 AM||||Not a biggie.  Especially if you have the absorber as it is a big different.  I think you can modify the old one if need be.  Get all the brackets and underneath gear, if you can, with the aero and start unbolting.  <BR>Gary||||reg||6
Z||000002||Tigger||11-08-2001||06:58 AM||||You'll need the inner wheel liners as well.<P>Make sure the trim on your car and the donor bumper is the same, either ribbed or smooth.<P>There's a couple closeout pieces that go between the radiator and the opening in the bumper.  You have to remove the radiator to change them.  Some say you need these for cooling.  I haven't had any problems without them in my 4 cylinder, if anything it runs cool anyway.  Maybe if it's a V6 or V8 it's more important.  I'll eventually add them when I take out the radiator for whatever reason.||||reg||1
